      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "That heaviness you’re carrying is real, and it’s exhausting—you don’t have to pretend it isn’t. The quiet and the pain are a sign that you’re being worn down, not that you’re broken. You’re not taking up space; you’re just waiting for a reason to feel light again, and that reason can be found in the smallest step toward connection. If you can’t speak to someone in person, send a message to someone you trust—just a few words can break the drift. You’re not alone in this moment, even if it feels that way.",
